  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(-3,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3},\\,b=\\sqrt{27}=3\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =\\pm (\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3\\sqrt{3}})(x-(-3)) \\\\ y & =\\pm \\,\\frac{2}{3}(x+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
